# The measured warm-up for this stand, in one place, because a constant re-typed per script drifts.
#
# Sourced by the runners:  . "$(dirname "$0")/warmup.env"
#
# Measured 2026-09-20 (bench/profile/results/warmup-gate.md): after 90 s of load, level-4
# compilation of application, Ktor, Exposed and serialiser code goes quiet for 160 s, 180 s and
# 100 s on the three database endpoints - so the brief's "no C2 compilation for 60 seconds" is met
# on all three, with margin.
#
# It is met only for THAT scope. Counting every compilation at every level, C2 never goes quiet at
# all: 1-19 events per 10 s for the whole window, which is the same fact 1.20 reports as 4.9-6.1 %
# of request CPU in compiler threads. The brief does not say which scope its gate means, and the two
# readings do not agree - the same shape of hole as the RQ0 gate (D1, B-53).
BENCH_WARMUP=${BENCH_WARMUP:-90}
